  "cli_result_text": "Submitted. Summary of the dependency findings that drove the file selection:\n\n**next.js \u2192 babel (real edge, direct source-level consumption):**\n- `packages/next/package.json` declares `@babel/core`, `@babel/traverse`, `@babel/types`, `@babel/generator`, and a suite of `@babel/plugin-*`/`@babel/preset-*` packages as `devDependencies` (they get bundled into `next/dist/compiled/babel/*` via the `ncc-compiled`/taskr build, not left as loose runtime deps).\n- `packages/next/src/build/babel/preset.ts` and `packages/next/src/build/babel/loader/index.ts` are the actual consumers \u2014 Next's custom `.babelrc` fallback path parses/transforms user code with this vendored Babel, walking the AST via `@babel/traverse`/`@babel/types`. A new `DecoratorMetadata` node reaches this code directly.\n- Root `package.json` also pins `@babel/core`, `@babel/parser`, `@babel/types`, `@babel/traverse` under `resolutions`, confirming the version-pin surface.\n\n**next.js \u2192 webpack (real edge, but irrelevant to this change):**\n- `packages/next/src/build/webpack-config.ts` imports `webpack` from `next/dist/compiled/webpack/webpack` \u2014 Next vendors its own webpack copy. This edge exists but carries no Babel-AST exposure.\n\n**webpack \u2192 babel (expected edge that does NOT hold):**\n- `webpack/package.json` lists `@babel/core`, `@babel/preset-react`, and `babel-loader` only under `devDependencies` (used for webpack's own example/test builds), never in `dependencies`.\n- `lib/javascript/JavascriptParser.js` proves webpack's actual runtime parser is `require(\"acorn\")`, not Babel. Webpack never touches a Babel AST at runtime \u2014 `babel-loader` is a separate, unvendored npm package outside this repo's blast radius.\n\nThis gives the topology: **babel \u2192 next.js (direct, breaking-change-relevant)**, and **webpack sits outside the Babel parser's reach** despite superficially looking like a natural target for a \"JS compilation pipeline\" rollout.",
